   "caption": "Day 9 and still no feedback? That's not a client problem. It's a missing clause.\n\n3 myths that keep you waiting:\n1. \"Waiting is part of the job.\" Fact: put a review window in the SOW.\n2. \"Silence means yes.\" Fact: only if your contract says so. Otherwise they choose: approve, a new date, or cut scope.\n3. \"More reviewers, better work.\" Fact: one named approver + a backup, one combined list of notes per round.\n\nThe clause (example terms, not legal advice):\n- Review window: 3 business days per round\n- One named approver + a backup\n- One combined list of notes per round\n- Late notes move the delivery date\n\nSave this for your next SOW. Send it to the friend still waiting on feedback.\n\n#agencylife #freelancetips #clientmanagement #socialmediamanager #creatorbusiness #freelancer",
   "keyword": null,
   "topic": "Client feedback myths vs facts: 3-business-day review window, deemed approval vs choice (approve/new date/cut scope), one approver + backup, one combined notes list",
   "pillar": 3,
   "sources": [
    "https://agencymanagementinstitute.com/do-you-have-a-feedback-approval-clause-in-your-sows/",
    "https://enterprisedna.co/resources/guides/agencies-stop-client-approval-delays",
    "https://blog.freelancersunion.org/2014/02/19/what-do-your-client-slow-respond/"
   ]
